-[Katherine] Of course.

72
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:21,910
I mean, I tried calling Richard,
but he's in Barcelona?

73
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:25,371
Has he been here at all this summer?

74
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:27,665
Off and on.

75
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:31,711
But Danny was here for a month,
and then there's the housekeeper

76
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:34,881
and Al, the doorman. It's been fine.

77
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:38,426
Jackie, if you wanted to stay here
in the city, I think I would understand.

78
00:03:38,509 --> 00:03:40,345
-But Vermont?
-[Jackie] It's a good school.

79
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:45,058
And I don't know, I… I just thought
that maybe somewhere new would be good.

80
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:47,518
But I thought everything was going okay.
You seemed happy.

81
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,062
It was. I was.

82
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:51,981
Then… did something happen?

83
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:56,194
With Alex or… maybe somebody else?

84
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:59,030
No. No. I just… I just

85
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:01,282
had to leave.

86
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:05,912
I wanted to get out of Silver Falls.
I just wanted to go home, to New York,

87
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,414
to before… everything.

88
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:10,750
But this isn't home anymore.

89
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:17,590
I, uh…

90
00:04:18,299 --> 00:04:21,261
I met some of my old friends,
you know, when I first got back.

91
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:25,056
But… everything's changed.

92
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:27,850
Our lives are just so different now.

93
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:34,107
And I tried to go to some places
that I used to go to with Lucy

94
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:39,487
and my mom and my dad,
like The Cloisters and Lincoln Center,

95
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:43,032
but it's just not the same without them.

96
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:45,159
[emotional music playing]

97
00:04:46,619 --> 00:04:48,037
It just made me realize

98
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:51,040
that I don't belong here anymore.

99
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:54,877
I don't belong anywhere.

100
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:59,590
So… I just need to find somewhere new.
Start fresh.

101
00:05:03,594 --> 00:05:04,971
Your mom and I used to come here

102
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:07,056
when one of us
was really going through something.

103
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:11,227
Like a breakup or if we flunked a test.

104
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:14,397
Although that was mostly me
because your mom never flunked anything.

105
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,401
And we figured out
that there was nothing we couldn't solve

106
00:05:18,484 --> 00:05:21,988
without enough butter
and chocolate and talking.

107
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:24,407
I'm glad she had you to talk to.

108
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:26,367
[Katherine] I'm afraid
I did most of the talking.

109
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,370
Your mom was such a good listener.

110
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:35,710
They say you choose your family,
and Angelica and I definitely did that.

111
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:40,465
All of us, Jackie.

112
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:43,843
Me, George, the kids,
we still want to be your family.

113
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:46,054
Whatever happened, we can fix it.

114
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,807
We want you to come home to us.

115
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:54,437
I just don't know if I can.

116
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:01,944
Okay, well, I'm gonna be there
for you no matter what.

117
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:04,155
If you want to go to Vermont,
I'll just come see you.

118
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:06,491
I mean, who doesn't love
the Green Mountain State?

119
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:13,039
You do belong, Jackie.

120
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:16,417
With us.

121
