00:07:17,061 --> 00:07:18,020
♪ But if-- ♪

141
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,021
[car engine stops]

142
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,357
It's gonna be okay. [sighs]

143
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:24,235
And if it's not, you tell me, okay?

144
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:26,696
Okay. [chuckles]

145
00:07:26,779 --> 00:07:29,282
She say anything to you about coming back?

146
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:31,409
I haven't spoken to her
since I left New York,

147
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:33,953
but it's a good thing
she's here though, yeah?

148
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:47,717
Danny, can you give me a hand?

149
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,267
-[Isaac] Let's go.
-Jackie!

150
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:58,352
I want you to meet Gregory Peck.

151
00:07:58,436 --> 00:08:00,229
Okay… Who? What?

152
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:01,522
It's his chicken.

153
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:03,900
I've raised him since a baby.

154
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:05,193
Chick, Benny.

155
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:06,903
-Gregory's a girl.
-Does it matter?

156
00:08:06,986 --> 00:08:08,571
It does if you want some eggs.

157
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:10,948
All right, come on, guys.
Let's go. Come on.

158
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:14,660
Red, 60!

159
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,954
-[Jordan] Isaac, over here!
-[Benny] Come on, you guys!

160
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:17,872
[Isaac] Say hut!

161
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,542
Jordan!

162
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:23,669
[Lee] Let's go!

163
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:25,546
-Let's go, Jordan!
-[Jordan] Thanks, man.

164
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:27,215
[Isaac] Run! Run! Run!

165
00:08:29,383 --> 00:08:31,177
[Benny] Jordan! Here!

166
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,515
[sighs softly]

167
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:39,018
[Benny] Jordan!

168
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,354
[Isaac] Outstanding.

169
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:43,022
-That's good.
-[Katherine] Hi!

170
00:08:43,105 --> 00:08:43,981
Hey.

171
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,274
Oh, Jackie!

172
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,527
Oh, welcome back.

173
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,403
-[Katherine] Missed you.
-We missed you.

174
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:50,488
Thanks, George.

175
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:53,658
Hi, Parker.

176
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:56,661
Hi, Jackie. Welcome home.

177
00:08:57,161 --> 00:08:58,120
It's good to see you.

178
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:00,915
Yeah.

179
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:03,042
You too.

180
00:09:04,418 --> 00:09:06,546
-Hey, we'll finish later.
-[Parker] Mm-hmm.

181
00:09:07,463 --> 00:09:09,924
Okay, I guess I'll go unpack.

182
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:12,009
[Katherine] If you need anything,
let me know.

183
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:15,263
Hey, how'd it go?

184
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:17,056
Well, she's here.

185
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,100
Did she say why she left?

186
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:22,937
Not exactly, but I think we both know
it had something to do with Alex and Cole.

187
00:09:24,063 --> 00:09:25,773
Well, let's hope
they can all get past that.

188
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:28,109
I think I just need
to spend more time with her.

189
00:09:28,859 --> 00:09:30,194
We'll keep an eye on her.

190
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:33,864
-We're gonna keep an eye on all of them.
-Hey, you want tea?

191
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,199
Yes, please.

192
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:39,662
I was going to send it,

193
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:43,124
but I figured I'd keep it here
for when you came back.

194
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:45,334
Thanks, Nathan.

195
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:47,420
[horse whinnies]

196
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:50,673
We really missed you.

197
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:51,591
Skylar too.

198
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:56,721
-How is he?
-You know, he's… Sky.

199
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:58,347
[chuckles]

200
00:09:58,431 --> 00:09:59,265
And Grace?

201
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:01,851
Oh, we didn't really see her
that much over the summer.

202
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:05,271
Please tell me you brought back
those mini-babkas from Zabar's.

203
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:08,941
-They are hands down the best thing--
-The best thing that you've ever tasted?

204
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,401
Yeah, I know. [chuckles]

205
00:10:10,484 --> 00:10:12,612
It's all he's talked about
since you got back.

206
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:15,114
-That's not all.
-Right, the movies at IFC.

207
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:18,659
How could I forget? And the eggs Benny
at that diner on 4th Street

208
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:21,245
and Jane's Carousel
and the Roosevelt Island Tramway--

209
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:22,413
It is really cool.

210
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:24,123
I didn't forget.

211
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:25,750
Thank you. That's awesome.

212
00:10:26,542 --> 00:10:28,919
-Can I try some?
-No way. These are mine.

213
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:30,755
Wow. Well, I'm glad you're back, Jackie.

214
00:10:30,838 --> 00:10:33,215
At least somebody can
I heart New York with him.

215
00:10:34,008 --> 00:10:34,842
Hey!

216
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:37,178
-[chuckles]
-[Danny scoffs]

217
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:38,638
So, you miss it?

218
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:39,847
Yeah.

219
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:43,601
Yeah, I… I do.
But it's good to be home too, so…

220
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:46,020
Was Richard sad to see you go?

221
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:49,398
I guess. But he's been pretty busy,

222
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:53,486
so I know he's glad
I came here instead of Vermont.

223
00:10:54,236 --> 00:10:55,154
And what about you?

224
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:57,323
Are you glad that you came here
instead of Vermont?

225
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:01,577
It's weird how familiar it is to be back,

226
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:04,330
but then it still doesn't feel like home.

227
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:06,707
Not yet, anyway.

228
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:09,085
You know, it was hard for everyone

229
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:10,753
with you leaving.

230
00:11:10,836 --> 00:11:13,005
But everybody's glad you're back.

231
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:14,256
Everybody?

232
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:19,261
Yeah, some may take
a little more warming up than others.

233
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:21,389
It'll be okay.

234
00:11:23,224 --> 00:11:25,226
[emotional music playing]

235
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:37,613
You okay, P?

236
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,535
She never even said goodbye.

237
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:49,166
She had her reasons.

238
00:11:57,883 --> 00:11:59,677
It's okay that you missed her.

239
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:11,272
[chuckles]

240
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,858
Come on. Take it easy on me.

241
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:16,110
-[Parker] You're just mad that I'm better.
-[Cole scoffs]

242
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:17,319
[Parker chuckles]

243
00:12:29,623 --> 00:12:31,834
[rooster crows]

244
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:38,340
[chicken clucking]

245
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:39,717
[horse whinnies]

246
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:47,433
Hi.

247
00:12:48,517 --> 00:12:49,435
[Alex] Hey.

248
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:55,024
So, uh,

249
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:58,569
how was Montana?

250
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:02,198
Pretty much just like here.
Horses and mountains.

251
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:08,412
Alex, I, uh…

252
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:10,247
I got you this.

253
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:16,796
The guy at the bookstore said if you like
sci-fi fantasy, then this is the bomb.

254
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:19,006
It's a new series.

255
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,801
Uh, thanks.

256
00:13:22,384 --> 00:13:25,387
I'm not really into fantasy anymore.

257
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:30,810
Alex, about when I left.

258
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:33,938
-I just want to explain.
-It's okay. It's fine. I know.

259
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:35,773
I messed up.

260
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:37,900
Shouldn't have, uh, said what I said.

261
00:13:37,983 --> 00:13:40,486
-No, it wasn't because of that--
-[Alex] It doesn't matter.

262
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:42,363
You left, and now you're back.

263
00:13:42,863 --> 00:13:43,697
[Jackie] Yeah, but--

264
00:13:43,781 --> 00:13:46,325
Look, I really gotta put Murphy away
before school, okay?

265
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,036
Okay.

266
00:13:58,212 --> 00:13:59,338
Alex…

267
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,218
Are we okay?

268
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,763
Sure. We're fine.

269
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:23,320
-Morning, Jackie.
-[Jackie] Morning.

270
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,238
Hey.

271
00:14:24,321 --> 00:14:26,448
So, there's, um… there's toast.

272
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:27,867
-Thanks.
-And…

273
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:31,203
They moved Parker's football practice
to the community center park this year?

274
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:36,041
Yes, and it's at the same time as Benny's
swim class on the other side of town.

275
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:37,710
I can finish those.

276
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:41,005
-No, no, no. I got this. It's fine.
-Honestly, Katherine, let me help.

277
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:42,715
-Okay. Thank you.
-Please.

278
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:44,592
Hey, honey.

279
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,304
I have my Ag Soc meeting
today in Lockwood.

280
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:52,057
Okay, well, maybe I can
drop Parker off at football

281
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:56,270
after I take Jordan to the film club,
and then I can swing back and get Benny?

282
00:14:56,353 --> 00:14:58,814
Benny's practice will be over by then.
You'll never make that.

283
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:01,108
-I could just bike over there.
-[both] No!

284
00:15:01,191 --> 00:15:03,986
[Katherine] Why did they move football?
We made it work last year.

285
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:04,904
I don't know.

286
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:07,656
Sweetie, I don't know
if I'll figure this out by practice.

287
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,909
But they'll pick all the teams this week.

288
00:15:11,118 --> 00:15:13,203
-Okay, who wants eggs?
-We will figure something out.

289
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,247
-[Benny] I do!
-[Lee] Yeah, but not too runny.

290
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,084
Excuse me.

291
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,212
[George] Hey, Cole, Danny,

292
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,924
can one of you guys take Parker
to her football practice later?

293
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,800
I can't. I have a study group.

294
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:27,760
[dish clatters]

295
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:31,472
What?

296
00:15:34,683 --> 00:15:35,517
Danny?

297
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:37,937
I mean, sure,
but I'd miss the sign-up for drama club,

298
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,647
and they hand out
the scene partners today.

299
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,274
Oh, we need more drivers in this family.

300
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:45,194
-Hey, we will get you there.
-Okay.

301
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:48,781
I know. I'm gonna call Will.
Maybe he can get you there.

302
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:50,282
[Jackie] Guys, here's your lunch.

303
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:52,618
Okay, whose job was it to get eggs today?

304
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:54,411
-Not me. I did it Friday.
-Not me.

305
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:56,622
-I'm pretty sure it was Jordan.
-[Jordan] Shut up, man.

306
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:01,377
If you guys want to eat this morning,
somebody better go get more eggs.

307
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,836
And I gotta go. Bye, everyone.

308
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,837
I'll go.

309
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,304
[Cole] Need any help?

310
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:16,308
No. I'm good.

311
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:18,352
Thanks.

312
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:27,444
Jackie, can you stop for a second?

313
00:16:27,945 --> 00:16:29,446
[emotional music playing]

314
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:35,035
I should get these to Danny.

315
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:48,549
Found it.

316
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:50,592
-Oh, thanks.
-Yeah.

317
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:53,095
Hey, make sure you water Friedrich, okay?

318
00:16:53,595 --> 00:16:54,596
Friedrich?

319
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,515
-My ficus.
-Right.

320
00:16:56,598 --> 00:16:59,435
But not too much. I don't want you
to drown him. I wrote it all down.

321
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:00,352
[Will] Got it.

322
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,104
Okay.

323
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:07,776
Phone, wallet, passport, boarding pass.

324
00:17:12,448 --> 00:17:13,615
What's the matter?

325
00:17:14,324 --> 00:17:15,451
-I don't wanna go.
-What?

326
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:16,368
No.

327
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:17,703
Of course you do.

328
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:20,247
Come on, a whole semester in Chile?

329
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,875
Up to your elbows
in soil for three months.

330
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:24,376
-This is your dream.
-[chuckles]

331
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,131
Come with me.

332
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:34,178
Hayles, we've been over this.

333
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:36,430
What am I gonna do

334
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:40,601
stuck on a biodynamic farm
in the middle of nowhere in Chile

335
00:17:40,684 --> 00:17:42,478
while you work on your thesis?

336
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:43,437
Yeah.

337
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:46,231
Plus, I got the ranch development
to keep me busy here.

338
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:47,149
I know.

339
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:49,026
I know. You're right.

340
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,237
I'm gonna miss you.

341
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:54,406
Me too.

342
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,620
-It's not even three months, right? So…
-Yeah.

343
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:01,413
-You'll be back before you know it.
-Yes.

344
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:05,167
Well, unless I meet,
like, a hot Chilean farmhand.

345
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,794
-Yeah, don't do that.
-I don't know.

346
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,754
I'll make no promises. [chuckles]

347
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:11,006
All right. We should get going. Come on.

348
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:11,965
Okay. Hold on.

349
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:16,553
We have, like, 20 minutes.

350
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:20,057
[giggles]

351
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:31,693
[gasps] Oh my God, Jackie! Hi!

352
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:34,238
Oh, I missed you!

353
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:36,698
-Hi, Grace.
-It's been so dead here this summer.

354
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:39,201
I almost joined my mom's prayer group
for company. [chuckles]

355
00:18:39,284 --> 00:18:42,204
-You didn't hang out with Skylar?
-Um, no. Not really.

356
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:44,540
He and Nathan have been
in their own little bubble of love.

357
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:49,628
You know? So I, um, helped out
at the church. I did a ton of babysitting.

358
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:52,131
I'm sorry we didn't talk
a whole lot this summer.

359
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:53,549
That's okay. [chuckles]

360
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:56,135
You could make it up to me
by telling me everything.

361
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:58,262
So what's it like being back?
Are you still with Alex?

362
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:00,013
'Cause everybody's talking about it.

363
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:01,557
It's complicated.

364
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:03,267
Complicated how?

365
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:08,021
Wait. Wait.

366
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:11,400
What?

367
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:13,652
He told me he loved me
at Will and Haley's wedding.

368
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:17,489
[scoffs] Jackie!
Oh my God! What did you say?

369
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:21,368
-Nothing. He had been drinking, so--
-[Grace] So you didn't say it back?

370
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:22,953
Well, I didn't know what to say.

371
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:25,831
Alex is so sweet,

372
00:19:25,914 --> 00:19:28,083
and being with him was so nice.

373
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:29,543
But then Cole…

374
00:19:30,127 --> 00:19:31,336
Cole what?

375
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,131
I found out he had fixed
Lucy's broken teapot.

376
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,800
He had kept it for me
since Thanksgiving. And then…

377
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:39,386
And then what? You made tea?
Like, come on!

378
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:43,140
We… we kissed.

379
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:45,809
-You kissed Cole Walter?!
-Sh!

380
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:47,936
Jackie, oh my God. But you were…

381
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:49,855
Weren't you still with Alex?

382
00:19:50,814 --> 00:19:51,940
Does he know?

383
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:56,111
Wow, Jackie. That's--

384
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:59,364
I know. I know. I messed up so bad.

385
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,782
[Grace sighs]

386
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:02,534
So, are you with Cole now?

387
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:04,369
No. What? No.

388
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:05,662
Do you wanna be?

389
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:06,997
Grace, no.

390
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:09,666
And anyway, it doesn't matter what I want.

391
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:12,377
What's important is
making things right with everyone.

392
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:14,755
What does that mean?
What are you gonna do?

393
00:20:14,838 --> 00:20:17,633
Well, first I'm gonna get into
driver's ed 'cause I need my license.

394
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:20,802
-I thought New Yorkers didn't drive.
-I'm not a New Yorker anymore.

395
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:23,513
Then I'm gonna have to
make things right with Alex.

396
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:26,892
Too mopey.

397
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:29,311
[rock music playing]

398
00:20:35,192 --> 00:20:36,568
It'll be fine.

399
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:38,445
Sure it will.

400
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:42,324
[phone pings]

401
00:20:43,992 --> 00:20:46,787
You've been doing that all morning.
Who is that?

402
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,456
-Danny.
-Danny Walter?

403
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:51,583
We've been texting
a little over the summer.

404
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:54,711
And what does his twin brother
think about that?

405
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:58,257
Ugh. The days of me caring
about what Cole Walter thinks

406
00:20:58,340 --> 00:20:59,841
are well and truly over.

407
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:00,801
Hmm.

408
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:04,596
[Tara] Come in.

409
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:06,974
Jackie!

410
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:09,476
Oh! It's good to have you back. Come in.

411
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:11,019
-Thanks.
-[Tara] Sit.

412
00:21:11,728 --> 00:21:13,897
So, you decided
against boarding school, huh?

413
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:16,275
The school requested your transcripts.

414
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:17,734
Oh, right. Yeah.

415
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:21,488
For the record,
I'm glad you decided to come back.

416
00:21:21,571 --> 00:21:23,282
Silver Falls is lucky to have you.

417
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:25,701
-Thank you.
-[Tara chuckles]

418
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:28,078
Um, I'm a little late choosing electives.

419
00:21:28,161 --> 00:21:30,580
Okay. Let's see here.

420
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,581
Um…

421
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:37,004
-Uh, yes. You don't have any.
-I'd really like to get into driver's ed.

422
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,256
Oh, I'm sorry, Jackie. It's full.

423
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:41,216
It's a super popular class.

424
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,551
Um…

425
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:45,887
The only elective still open is woodshop.

426
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:47,806
What?

427
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:51,935
Think of it this way.
The world will always need shelving.

428
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:58,025
So this is where guests will park,
then they'll walk to the yurts from here.

429
00:21:58,108 --> 00:21:59,943
-And um…
-Can we get the yurts out--

430
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:02,654
We'll need more horses,
so larger stables at some point?

431
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:05,532
Although I guess we could hire horses
on an ad hoc basis at first.

432
00:22:05,615 --> 00:22:07,284
We'll do the group cookouts here.

433
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:09,202
We have to get a liquor license.

434
00:22:09,286 --> 00:22:11,788
And we'll do the dark sky tours from here.

435
00:22:12,831 --> 00:22:14,166
Right. Um…

436
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:18,628
Well, hey, it's great. It's great.
You're obviously on top of it,

437
00:22:18,712 --> 00:22:20,881
but can we get the yurts out
to the back field?

438
00:22:20,964 --> 00:22:22,424
'Cause I don't want them there.

439
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:25,677
And, like, I don't know, dark sky tours.
Who's gonna do that?

440
00:22:25,761 --> 00:22:27,637
I mean, you and I
know nothing about astronomy.

441
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:31,058
Yeah, we'll get help for that,
which is another thing we have to discuss.

442
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:35,020
Staff. We budgeted for two full-time,
but I think four makes more sense.

443
00:22:35,103 --> 00:22:36,646
Four? [sighs]

444
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:39,566
Aren't we supposed to be
making money here and not spending it?

445
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:44,780
Or…

446
00:22:48,575 --> 00:22:53,038
So, can anyone tell me what a lathe is?

447
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:56,249
No?

448
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:58,543
Okay then. [sighs]

449
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:00,712
A lathe is used to turn wood,

450
00:23:01,296 --> 00:23:04,716
to make bowls, spindles,
legs for furniture.

451
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:08,095
Anything that needs to be rounded.

452
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:14,684
How did it go?

453
00:23:14,768 --> 00:23:15,769
[Nikhil] Well,

454
00:23:16,728 --> 00:23:20,732
as of next semester,
I am officially out of the job.

455
00:23:23,276 --> 00:23:25,028
Yeah, Ms. Elson
is back from her sabbatical,

456
00:23:25,112 --> 00:23:28,115
and technically I gave them notice,
so I'm on borrowed time.

457
00:23:28,698 --> 00:23:30,867
But you have a job for now, right?

458
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:34,496
Part-time. I'm doing, uh,
freshman Drama and English Lit.

459
00:23:34,579 --> 00:23:36,373
And I'm covering the newspaper club.

460
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:37,541
Well, that's something.

461
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:40,877
And who knows what can happen
in the next few months.

462
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:42,963
Look. [sighs]

463
00:23:43,630 --> 00:23:47,342
When I turned down that job in London,
I was not expecting I'd end up unemployed.

464
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:48,260
Hey.

465
00:23:49,136 --> 00:23:50,637
You're not unemployed.

466
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:53,598
Something else will turn up.

467
00:23:54,182 --> 00:23:55,183
Hey, um,

468
00:23:56,893 --> 00:23:59,563
you don't have to be
such a cheerleader all the time.

469
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:06,027
But… I… I believe in you.
And I know you're gonna do great.

470
00:24:07,237 --> 00:24:08,155
Okay, um,

471
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:11,950
I'm gonna go, uh, set up
the newspaper room, okay?

472
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:20,375
All right, this is driver's ed.
I'm Coach Allen.

473
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:21,960
Find a seat, please.

474
00:24:22,043 --> 00:24:23,211
Hey, Alex.

475
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:25,172
Can I sit here?

476
00:24:25,755 --> 00:24:27,048
Sure, yeah.

477
00:24:28,175 --> 00:24:29,176
Cool.

478
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:37,601
Driving, it's hard.

479
00:24:37,684 --> 00:24:39,811
-It was great.
-[coach] You need to focus.

480
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,814
Yes, pay attention, please. It's day one.

481
00:24:46,359 --> 00:24:47,277
Hey, you.

482
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:48,320
Hi.

483
00:24:48,904 --> 00:24:50,155
-Hi, Olivia.
-[Olivia] Hi.

484
00:24:51,448 --> 00:24:54,493
So… I want to join the paper.

485
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:56,703
What? Why?

486
00:24:56,786 --> 00:24:59,915
Well, my homeroom teacher was saying
we need to have more extracurriculars,

487
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:02,167
and I kind of only have band.

488
00:25:02,792 --> 00:25:04,044
Why the paper?

489
00:25:04,127 --> 00:25:06,421
Well, I like writing,
and I want to get better.

490
00:25:06,505 --> 00:25:09,424
And they wouldn't let me join last year
'cause I was a freshman.

491
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:12,010
But I thought maybe I'd have an in
with the new editor.

492
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:12,969
[chuckles]

493
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:16,223
The paper has to be really good this year.

494
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:19,851
I want to make it more serious,
do more in-depth pieces,

495
00:25:20,435 --> 00:25:23,355
rather than just covering
football games and student council.

496
00:25:23,438 --> 00:25:24,439
[Nathan] Mm-hmm.

497
00:25:25,482 --> 00:25:28,443
-You want to see the first edition?
-Now? Sure.

498
00:25:29,069 --> 00:25:32,239
-[chuckles]
-The school's had its budget cut by a lot.

499
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:35,450
And the arts are always the first to go
when money is tight.

500
00:25:35,992 --> 00:25:39,329
Band, drama, after-school activities,
they'll all be on the line.

501
00:25:40,330 --> 00:25:42,499
But I bet the football team
will be just fine.

502
00:25:42,582 --> 00:25:43,458
[laughs] Hmm.

503
00:25:44,459 --> 00:25:46,836
Wait, they won't cancel the fall formal,
will they?

504
00:25:47,671 --> 00:25:48,547
I hope not.

505
00:25:48,630 --> 00:25:52,175
But these cuts are a big deal.
I've done a special editorial on it.

506
00:25:52,259 --> 00:25:54,219
Hoping to add it
to my portfolio for Georgetown.

507
00:25:54,302 --> 00:25:57,514
Maybe I can help.
Be your unofficial assistant editor?

508
00:25:57,597 --> 00:25:58,598
[chuckles]

509
00:25:59,516 --> 00:26:01,977
You have a ways to go
before becoming assistant editor.

510
00:26:02,060 --> 00:26:02,894
Oh.

511
00:26:04,521 --> 00:26:07,899
Hey, if you're joining the paper,
I'm your boss, not your boyfriend.

512
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:10,652
Okay, boss.

513
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:11,695
[Skylar chuckles]

514
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:12,654
So, I'm in?

515
00:26:16,283 --> 00:26:18,702
Yeah. You're in.

516
00:26:18,785 --> 00:26:19,744
[chuckles]

517
00:26:21,121 --> 00:26:22,414
You're so excited.

518
00:26:22,497 --> 00:26:24,165
-I am excited.
-[laughs]

519
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:26,585
Okay, so you need to tell me
the difference between…

520
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:28,628
It's the first day.
You're supposed to teach us.

521
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:30,171
That's the whole point, you know?

522
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:34,426
What? You okay?

523
00:26:35,218 --> 00:26:37,679
Yeah. I just didn't know
he knew Ruby that well.

524
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:44,936
-I thought you needed to get your books.
-I'll get 'em later.

525
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:55,822
♪ I'm still putting booze
In my apple juice… ♪

526
00:26:55,905 --> 00:26:57,324
No, there's no way…

527
00:26:57,407 --> 00:26:58,325
[overlapping chatter]

528
00:26:58,408 --> 00:27:00,577
♪ I'm sad, I'm sad ♪

529
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:04,831
♪ Don't make me choose
'Cause it won't be you ♪

530
00:27:04,914 --> 00:27:08,710
♪ I got no excuse, I'm bad, I'm bad ♪

531
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:11,171
♪ Ask anyone who knows me ♪

532
00:27:11,254 --> 00:27:12,839
♪ Tell me not to, and I… ♪

533
00:27:12,922 --> 00:27:13,965
[Katherine] Guys,

534
00:27:14,549 --> 00:27:18,178
I just want to say how happy I am
that we're all here… together.

535
00:27:19,095 --> 00:27:22,015
And Alex and Danny,
we missed you so much this summer.

536
00:27:22,098 --> 00:27:23,933
Not me. I like the quiet.

537
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:25,518
[Katherine chuckles]

538
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:30,815
And Jackie…
we're so happy that you're home.

539
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:33,151
Yeah, I missed you, Jackie. Jackie's back!

540
00:27:33,234 --> 00:27:34,152
[Katherine chuckles]

541
00:27:34,235 --> 00:27:35,320
[all] To Jackie!

542
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:36,363
[Alex] To Jackie.

543
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:39,240
This is better
than boarding school, right?

544
00:27:39,741 --> 00:27:40,950
[Isaac] What did he say?

545
00:27:41,034 --> 00:27:43,286
[Nathan] She was gonna go
to boarding school?

546
00:27:46,414 --> 00:27:48,041
Hey, can I be excused for a sec?

547
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,504
Um, sure. Until the food comes.

548
00:27:52,587 --> 00:27:53,421
Thanks.

549
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:56,966
[overlapping chatter]

550
00:28:03,139 --> 00:28:04,140
Hey.

551
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:09,729
Cole, great play you gave Isaac
on the field today.

552
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:11,981
-Mm, no, that wasn't me.
-[coach] Come on.

553
00:28:12,065 --> 00:28:14,067
I know a Cole Walter play when I see it.

554
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:15,652
You know, if you're interested,

555
00:28:15,735 --> 00:28:18,488
the assistant coach position
is still available.

556
00:28:18,571 --> 00:28:20,907
Thanks. Yeah, I don't think so.

557
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:23,201
All right. Enjoy your evening.

558
00:28:25,245 --> 00:28:26,079
[George] Coach.

559
00:28:26,162 --> 00:28:27,956
-Good to see you. Bye.
-How are you?

560
00:28:28,039 --> 00:28:29,165
[Katherine] Hi.

561
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:31,167
[chuckles]

562
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:35,964
Danny, what are you thinking?

563
00:28:36,047 --> 00:28:38,258
-No phones at the table.
-Sorry.

564
00:28:38,341 --> 00:28:41,386
He's been texting some girl back
in New York ever since he got home.

565
00:28:41,469 --> 00:28:42,595
Oh!

566
00:28:42,679 --> 00:28:45,014
-[Parker] Finally, some pizza.
-Good for you, Danny boy.

567
00:28:45,598 --> 00:28:46,683
[George] Hey. Hey.

568
00:28:46,766 --> 00:28:49,853
-Yeah, maybe later.
-[Isaac] Our boy's growing up!

569
00:28:50,353 --> 00:28:52,856
-[Benny] The breadsticks will be better…
-If I did, I would.

570
00:28:53,773 --> 00:28:54,774
Yeah. Thank you.

571
00:28:54,858 --> 00:28:56,484
I gotta get strong.

572
00:28:57,652 --> 00:29:00,447
♪ When everything feels like yesterday ♪

573
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:06,786
♪ Can't live with myself
I can't think of us ♪

574
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,956
♪ Find somebody else
I feel like I'm drunk ♪

575
00:29:10,039 --> 00:29:13,293
♪ Tell me I'm right so I can stay away ♪

576
00:29:13,376 --> 00:29:15,086
♪ Stay away… ♪

577
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:17,172
Hey, you need anything?

578
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,008
No, thanks.

579
00:29:21,009 --> 00:29:22,177
You okay?

580
00:29:22,927 --> 00:29:23,762
Yeah.

581
00:29:24,262 --> 00:29:25,722
Just, you know,

582
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:27,807
adjusting.

583
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:30,935
♪ You see I'm lighting out your spark
And I'm leaving scars ♪

584
00:29:31,019 --> 00:29:31,853
♪ I didn't mean to ♪

585
00:29:31,936 --> 00:29:33,396
♪ Dancing with my fire… ♪

586
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:36,107
I don't know what happened to him
over the summer, but…

587
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:37,025
He's changed?

588
00:29:38,359 --> 00:29:39,611
And not in a good way.

589
00:29:45,074 --> 00:29:47,243
I've been texting this girl lately…

590
00:29:48,036 --> 00:29:50,038
[cricket chirping]

591
00:29:56,294 --> 00:29:57,378
[knock on door]

592
00:29:58,171 --> 00:29:59,005
It's open.

593
00:30:01,090 --> 00:30:02,091
Hi.

594
00:30:03,134 --> 00:30:06,763
I thought I'd just check in with you.
I know today was a little tricky, huh?

595
00:30:06,846 --> 00:30:08,848
[Jackie] Yeah.
I guess it will take a while.

596
00:30:08,932 --> 00:30:11,684
And I tried to get into driver's ed today,
and it was full.

597
00:30:12,936 --> 00:30:15,063
-You want to learn how to drive?
-[Jackie] Yeah.

598
00:30:15,146 --> 00:30:17,982
I want to help you and George with
the younger kids and their activities.

599
00:30:18,066 --> 00:30:20,860
Oh, Jackie, you're so thoughtful.

600
00:30:21,653 --> 00:30:24,489
And yeah, it would be amazing
to have another driver around here,

601
00:30:24,572 --> 00:30:26,074
but that's not your job.

602
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:31,830
You don't have to be useful to be welcome.

603
00:30:31,913 --> 00:30:34,582
I wanna contribute,
be a part of the family.

604
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:36,084
[Katherine] You already are.

605
00:30:37,377 --> 00:30:40,547
Listen, it was hard on everybody knowing
that you didn't want to be around us,

606
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:42,340
even for a little while.

607
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:44,843
And we get that you needed some space,

608
00:30:44,926 --> 00:30:48,054
but some people are going to have
their feelings about that,

609
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:50,390
and that might take a little time.

610
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:56,980
And I'm sorry I made it seem like
it was gonna be easy to come back here.

611
00:30:58,481 --> 00:30:59,315
It isn't.

612
00:31:00,108 --> 00:31:01,276
And I see that now.

613
00:31:04,153 --> 00:31:06,155
But if anybody can do hard things,

614
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:07,824
it's you.

615
00:31:07,907 --> 00:31:09,909
[emotional music playing]

616
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:20,044
[upbeat music playing]

617
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:30,305
Hey, Brandon?

618
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:32,599
I was just wondering
if you'd switch electives with me?

619
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:35,810
Can't. I need my license
so I can help my dad with deliveries.

620
00:31:42,775 --> 00:31:44,193
Hi, Maria.

621
00:31:44,819 --> 00:31:46,279
I'm not leaving driver's ed, Jackie.

622
00:31:50,199 --> 00:31:51,117
Uh, Jackie?

623
00:31:53,244 --> 00:31:54,495
I'll switch with you.

624
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:56,873
Really? You sure?

625
00:31:58,082 --> 00:32:00,251
I've got my bike.
I'll do it in the spring.

626
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:01,252
Thank you.

627
00:32:01,336 --> 00:32:02,170
[Kiley] Yeah.

628
00:32:29,948 --> 00:32:30,949
Oh.

629
00:32:32,283 --> 00:32:33,618
Hi.

630
00:32:34,202 --> 00:32:35,036
Hey.

631
00:32:35,536 --> 00:32:38,164
Um, I… I didn't know
that you worked in here.

632
00:32:38,247 --> 00:32:40,625
[Erin] Well,
just when Ms. Levin is shorthanded.

633
00:32:41,668 --> 00:32:42,752
I like the quiet.

634
00:32:43,670 --> 00:32:44,712
Yeah, I know what you mean.

635
00:32:50,677 --> 00:32:52,387
Do you need help finding anything?

636
00:32:53,262 --> 00:32:54,347
No.

637
00:32:58,309 --> 00:32:59,602
Hey, Erin, um…

638
00:33:01,062 --> 00:33:02,397
I just, uh…

639
00:33:03,856 --> 00:33:05,775
When I texted that I missed you,

640
00:33:06,734 --> 00:33:07,568
I meant it.

641
00:33:08,695 --> 00:33:09,779
So did I.

642
00:33:12,115 --> 00:33:14,283
[emotional music playing]

643
00:33:42,437 --> 00:33:44,188
Oh, hey, Jackie. Welcome.

644
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:47,817
We're working in pairs today,
just going over basic driving principles,

645
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:49,193
so just find a seat.

646
00:33:52,071 --> 00:33:54,449
I want you to think
of a steering wheel like a clock.

647
00:33:54,532 --> 00:33:56,492
-A clock tells you what time it is.
-Talk later.

648
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:59,620
Alex, you're late. Please, take a seat.

649
00:34:07,503 --> 00:34:12,425
As I was saying, the rules have changed,
but one thing that hasn't is your safety.

650
00:34:12,508 --> 00:34:16,554
Texting, putting makeup on,
eating, daydreaming,

651
00:34:16,637 --> 00:34:18,556
all of these things can cause accidents.

652
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:20,641
[tools whirring]

653
00:34:23,686 --> 00:34:25,521
Hey, um, Kiley, right?

654
00:34:28,274 --> 00:34:29,442
How'd you end up in here?

655
00:34:30,026 --> 00:34:31,444
Somebody let me down.

656
00:34:34,864 --> 00:34:36,574
Uh, so this is a lathe.

657
00:34:36,657 --> 00:34:38,034
And, uh, what you need to do--

658
00:34:38,117 --> 00:34:41,579
Thanks. I know how to use a lathe.
Used it before.

659
00:34:43,164 --> 00:34:43,998
Great.

660
00:34:44,624 --> 00:34:46,375
You know you're holding it
upside down, right?

661
00:34:51,380 --> 00:34:52,423
[scoffs]

662
00:34:52,507 --> 00:34:53,424
Obviously.

663
00:34:53,508 --> 00:34:54,425
[scoffs]

664
00:34:58,513 --> 00:34:59,347
Okay.

665
00:35:01,849 --> 00:35:05,228
You're supposed to check
your rearview mirror and your side mirror.

666
00:35:05,728 --> 00:35:06,771
Okay.

667
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:09,899
Did you check your blind spot?

668
00:35:09,982 --> 00:35:10,858
[sighs]

669
00:35:11,776 --> 00:35:14,195
-You left the handbrake on.
-Do you want to drive?

670
00:35:14,278 --> 00:35:17,115
You two, you remind me of my grandparents.

671
00:35:18,699 --> 00:35:19,909
Rest in peace, Gigi.

672
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:22,286
Alex, can we talk?

673
00:35:22,370 --> 00:35:23,663
We are talking.

674
00:35:23,746 --> 00:35:26,124
-I need to know what's going on.
-We've been over this.

675
00:35:26,207 --> 00:35:29,460
I said what I said,
and you left without saying goodbye.

676
00:35:29,544 --> 00:35:32,046
So it seems pretty clear to me
that there's nothing going on.

677
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:33,589
-Alex…
-But you're right.

678
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:35,466
We never did officially break up.

679
00:35:35,550 --> 00:35:39,095
So if you need some kinda declaration,
let's call it now.

680
00:35:39,178 --> 00:35:40,179
What?

681
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:43,975
Time of death, September 6th,

682
00:35:45,268 --> 00:35:46,227
2:45.

683
00:35:48,312 --> 00:35:49,313
Happy?

684
00:35:49,397 --> 00:35:51,399
[emotional music playing]

685
00:35:59,115 --> 00:36:02,160
-Kiles. Kiley.
-Where's the entourage?

686
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:03,995
Mm, uh, what?

687
00:36:04,078 --> 00:36:05,830
Every time I've seen you
the past couple days,

688
00:36:05,913 --> 00:36:07,456
you've been surrounded by your harem.

689
00:36:07,540 --> 00:36:08,541
[whispers] I know.

690
00:36:09,041 --> 00:36:10,877
It's insane, Kiles.

691
00:36:11,669 --> 00:36:15,756
What's insane, Alex, is that
you would be so happy to become so…

692
00:36:16,716 --> 00:36:18,759
I don't know, just like everyone else.

693
00:36:20,094 --> 00:36:21,470
So what?

694
00:36:21,554 --> 00:36:23,931
Maybe I am happy
to be like everybody else.

695
00:36:24,557 --> 00:36:27,268
Maybe you should stop
trying so hard to be an outsider.

696
00:36:27,351 --> 00:36:29,312
Maybe then you wouldn't be
so angry all the time.

697
00:36:30,646 --> 00:36:31,689
I'm not angry all the time.

698
00:36:31,772 --> 00:36:32,732
[Alex] Mm, really?

699
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:36,152
Then why'd you leave driver's ed?
Now I'm stuck with Jackie as a partner.

700
00:36:36,235 --> 00:36:38,613
We signed up
for driver's ed together, remember?

701
00:36:38,696 --> 00:36:39,530
-Yeah.
-[Kiley] Yeah.

702
00:36:39,614 --> 00:36:42,074
And that first class,
you ditched me for some random girl.

703
00:36:42,658 --> 00:36:44,327
-You mean Maria?
-[Kiley] Whoever.

704
00:36:44,410 --> 00:36:47,288
The point is,
we were gonna do it together,

705
00:36:47,371 --> 00:36:49,415
and now we're not.
Okay? And that's on you.

706
00:36:49,498 --> 00:36:52,126
She asked to sit there.
I didn't think it was a big deal.

707
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:54,545
Yeah, you're right, Alex. It isn't.

708
00:36:54,629 --> 00:36:55,463
[Alex scoffs]

709
00:36:57,340 --> 00:36:58,216
[scoffs]

710
00:36:58,966 --> 00:37:01,552
Oh, yeah. Not angry at all.

711
00:37:15,399 --> 00:37:16,234
Parker?

712
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:18,444
Can I talk to you for a second?

713
00:37:22,365 --> 00:37:24,492
I just want to apologize for leaving

714
00:37:25,326 --> 00:37:27,245
and for not staying in touch all summer.

715
00:37:28,246 --> 00:37:29,455
I really missed you.

716
00:37:34,210 --> 00:37:38,631
And now that I'm back,
I'm really gonna try to be there for you.

717
00:37:40,675 --> 00:37:44,637
And that includes
getting my driver's license

718
00:37:44,720 --> 00:37:47,848
so I can take you
to football practice and other things.

719
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:49,684
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

720
00:37:50,476 --> 00:37:52,311
I'd be like your own personal chauffeur.

721
00:37:52,395 --> 00:37:54,397
[upbeat music playing]

722
00:37:56,232 --> 00:37:58,276
I… kinda missed you too.

723
00:38:02,738 --> 00:38:03,739
Let's see it.

724
00:38:09,328 --> 00:38:10,788
-Good try.
-It wasn't great.

725
00:38:10,871 --> 00:38:11,747
[laughs]

726
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:14,125
[Kiley] Thanks, guys.

727
00:38:14,208 --> 00:38:15,084
-See ya.
-Bye.

728
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:18,379
You hanging around
for more woodworking tips?

729
00:38:18,462 --> 00:38:21,590
[chuckles] My dad's not really into
family dinnertime, you know?

730
00:38:21,674 --> 00:38:22,508
Mm.

731
00:38:24,051 --> 00:38:27,471
Only time he talks to me is when it's
about football and how bad I am at it,

732
00:38:27,555 --> 00:38:30,766
and I just didn't really feel like
dealing with that tonight, so…

733
00:38:33,352 --> 00:38:34,895
Ooh, sorry for the overshare.

734
00:38:34,979 --> 00:38:35,938
-Um…
-[chuckles]

735
00:38:36,439 --> 00:38:38,274
I'm sure your parents are great, right?

736
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:40,693
I live with my grandma.

737
00:38:42,403 --> 00:38:43,404
[door opens]

738
00:38:44,030 --> 00:38:45,698
D! You all on your lonesome?

739
00:38:45,781 --> 00:38:48,534
Oh, just, uh, late-night munchies,
if you know what I mean.

740
00:38:48,617 --> 00:38:50,578
Get me an extra hot pepperoni
with three sodas.

741
00:38:50,661 --> 00:38:52,204
TJ, hey, just take it easy.

742
00:38:53,539 --> 00:38:55,041
We close in 20 minutes.

743
00:38:55,124 --> 00:38:56,334
We eat fast.

744
00:39:00,212 --> 00:39:01,464
So you can read now?

745
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:02,631
Yeah. [scoffs]

746
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:04,258
-Academics. You know me.
-[TJ] Science?

747
00:39:04,342 --> 00:39:05,176
Chemistry?

748
00:39:05,259 --> 00:39:08,054
[boy] Pizza shredder.
Insert here, am I right?

749
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:10,139
[uplifting music playing]

750
00:39:11,766 --> 00:39:12,641
[chuckles softly]

751
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:25,071
What's making you so happy?

752
00:39:26,947 --> 00:39:29,075
Oh, nothing. Nothing.

753
00:39:33,954 --> 00:39:34,872
So, um,

754
00:39:36,290 --> 00:39:38,918
did you hear that Alex and Jackie
officially broke up?

755
00:39:42,088 --> 00:39:42,922
So?

756
00:39:43,005 --> 00:39:45,424
So, maybe you should go talk to her?

757
00:39:49,345 --> 00:39:50,262
I just, um…

758
00:39:51,555 --> 00:39:53,182
I know how much
she missed you this summer.

759
00:39:53,265 --> 00:39:55,267
["Let It Happen" playing]

760
00:39:58,896 --> 00:39:59,980
♪ No, I know… ♪

761
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:01,440
[horse whinnies]

762
00:40:01,524 --> 00:40:05,861
♪ I'm a walking contradiction
And it shows… ♪

763
00:40:07,363 --> 00:40:08,697
This was on the porch.

764
